 \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1912 CE:\r\n— fleet: 1."},{"id":"marker0","name":"Craftre Hot Springs","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 86°F."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Fomyard Healing Spring","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Blechwel — gold mining town","legend":"Blechwel is a mining town of 4018 people just nearby the gold mine."},{"id":"marker3","name":"The New Tavern","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious cured cabbage with green sap is served here."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Yeolivean Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Southambean Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Shifractham Waterfall","legend":"A gorgeous waterfall flows here."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Wargham Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Feny War. \r\nDate: December 13, 1735 Causbury Era."},{"id":"marker8","name":"Stanster Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Cambrighian War. \r\nDate: August 18, 1747 Causbury Era."},{"id":"marker9","name":"Mitbury Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Cambrighian Campaign. \r\nDate: March 30, 1907 Causbury Era."},{"id":"marker10","name":"Calingham Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Cambrighian War. \r\nDate: April 6, 1912 Causbury Era."},{"id":"marker11","name":"Bingraring Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Buclish Conflict. \r\nDate: May 6, 1473 Causbury Era."},{"id":"marker12","name":"Reasalworth Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Buclish Conflict. \r\nDate: October 18, 1471 Causbury Era."},{"